-- EXPECT-ERROR: `Cap(IO.FileWrite)` cannot be deserialized
-- Capability unforgeability (R3), derive over a record field (2026-08-05).
--
-- The record spelling of reject/t144. Kept as a separate file because the
-- derived record decoder and the derived variant decoder are built by
-- different branches of `expand_derive` (TDRecord vs TDVariant), so a check
-- wired into only one of them would still pass the other's test.
--
-- The narrower `IO.FileWrite` here rather than `IO` is deliberate: it proves
-- the rejection is about `Cap` appearing at all, not about the root
-- capability specifically.
mod DeriveRecordForge do
  needs IO

  type Handle = { id : Int, tok : Cap(IO.FileWrite) }
  derive Json for Handle

  fn main() do
    println("codec generated over a capability field")
  end
end
